B=[
("what-makes-a-website-truly-professional","What Makes a Website Truly Professional?","Web Design","2026-11-10","Professionalism is less about decoration and more about clarity, consistency and care.",[
("Clarity comes first",["A professional website tells a visitor what you do, who it is for and what to do next within a few seconds. If that takes effort, no amount of polish will rescue it.","Start with a single sentence that states your offer, and place the main action where people expect to find it."]),
("Consistency builds trust",["Fonts, colours, spacing and button styles should behave the same on every page. Inconsistency signals carelessness, even when visitors cannot say why the site feels off.","A small set of repeatable components does more for credibility than a large set of one-off effects."]),
("Details that people notice",["Pages that load quickly, text that is easy to read on a phone and forms that explain errors all communicate competence.","Check the unglamorous parts: broken links, missing image descriptions, outdated contact details and unclear page titles."])]),
("principles-of-modern-web-design","The Principles of Modern Web Design","Web Design","2026-11-03","Six durable principles that guide good layouts, whatever the trend of the year.",[
("Hierarchy guides the eye",["Size, weight, colour and spacing tell visitors what matters most. Give each page one clear focal point and let supporting content step back."]),
("Whitespace is a tool",["Empty space separates ideas and makes text easier to read. Crowded layouts feel cheaper and tire the reader sooner."]),
("Typography does the heavy lifting",["Most of a website is text. Choose one or two typefaces, keep line lengths comfortable and use a restrained size scale."]),
("Make it responsive and accessible",["Design for small screens first, keep contrast readable and make every action reachable by keyboard. These are baseline expectations, not extras."])]),
("why-mobile-first-design-matters","Why Mobile-First Design Matters","Web Design","2026-10-27","Starting from the smallest screen forces better decisions about content.",[
("Constraints sharpen content",["A phone screen has room for one idea at a time. Designing for it first makes you decide what is essential before adding anything else."]),
("Touch changes the rules",["Fingers are less precise than cursors. Buttons need generous size and spacing, and menus must be easy to open and close one-handed."]),
("Scale up deliberately",["Once the mobile layout works, tablet and desktop versions can add columns and imagery where they help. They should not simply stretch the phone design."]),
("Test on real widths",["Resizing a desktop browser is not enough. Check common phone widths and look for text overflow, cramped buttons and images that crop badly."])]),
("how-much-should-a-business-website-cost","How Much Should a Business Website Cost?","Business Growth","2026-10-20","What drives the price of a website, and how to compare quotes fairly.",[
("What affects the price",["The main drivers are the number of pages, how much is custom design versus a template, the features needed (forms, bookings, payments) and how much content you supply yourself."]),
("Compare scope, not just totals",["Two quotes with different totals may include different things. Ask how many pages, how many revision rounds, what integrations and what happens after launch."]),
("Remember the running costs",["Domain registration, hosting and third-party services are usually separate from design fees. A good quote lists them so there are no surprises."]),
("Our own pricing",["Crestpane publishes its package prices and a calculator on the pricing page, and confirms every project in a written quote before work begins."])]),
("understanding-ui-and-ux","Understanding UI and UX","UI/UX","2026-10-13","They are related but different: one is how it looks, the other is how it works.",[
("User interface",["UI covers what people see and touch: layout, colour, type, buttons and icons. Good UI makes actions obvious and the brand recognisable."]),
("User experience",["UX covers the whole journey: whether people can find information, complete a task and feel confident doing it. It includes structure, wording and speed."]),
("Why you need both",["A beautiful interface on a confusing structure still fails, and a sound structure with a weak interface feels untrustworthy. Strong projects design both together."])]),
("website-design-mistakes-to-avoid","Website Design Mistakes to Avoid","Web Design","2026-10-06","Seven problems that quietly cost businesses enquiries.",[
("Unclear messaging",["If visitors cannot tell what you offer, they leave. Lead with plain language about what you do and for whom."]),
("Ignoring mobile",["Many visitors arrive on phones. Tiny text, hidden menus and sideways scrolling send them away."]),
("Slow, heavy pages",["Oversized images and unnecessary scripts delay everything. Compress images and load only what a page needs."]),
("Buried contact details",["Make the way to reach you visible on every page, and make forms short enough to complete."]),
("Inconsistent design",["Mixed fonts, colours and button styles make a site look unfinished. Define a small system and stick to it."])]),
("designing-better-landing-pages","Designing Better Landing Pages","Business Growth","2026-09-29","A landing page works when it asks for one thing and removes distractions.",[
("Pick one goal",["Decide the single action you want: call, book or request a quote. Every element should support it."]),
("Lead with the benefit",["The headline should state what the visitor gains. Follow with a short explanation and a clear button."]),
("Remove the exits",["Extra navigation and unrelated links pull attention away. Keep the page focused and the form short."]),
("Support the claim",["Use real examples, real photos and honest detail rather than invented numbers. If you have no proof yet, explain your process clearly instead."])]),
("e-commerce-user-experience","E-commerce User Experience","E-commerce","2026-09-22","How product pages, search and checkout shape whether people buy.",[
("Help people find things",["Clear categories, working search and sensible filters matter more than a clever homepage."]),
("Make product pages answer questions",["Good photos, honest descriptions, size or spec details and visible delivery information reduce hesitation."]),
("Keep checkout simple",["Ask only for what you need, show costs early and make errors easy to correct. Every extra field is a reason to abandon."])]),
("website-performance-and-speed","Website Performance and Speed","SEO","2026-09-15","Speed is part of the experience, and most gains come from basics.",[
("Start with images",["Large images are the most common cause of slow pages. Resize them to the size they are shown and use modern formats such as WebP."]),
("Ship less code",["Every script and font adds weight. Remove what the page does not use and load the rest only when needed."]),
("Measure, then change",["Test on a mid-range phone and a normal connection, change one thing at a time and compare. Scores vary, so look at trends rather than a single number."])]),
("choosing-the-right-website-structure","Choosing the Right Website Structure","Development","2026-09-08","One page, a few pages or a full site: how to decide.",[
("Match structure to the goal",["A single page suits a focused offer or a campaign. A business with several services usually needs a page for each so people can find them."]),
("Think in journeys",["List the questions a visitor has and the order they ask them. Your navigation should answer them in that order."]),
("Plan for growth",["Choose a structure that can add pages later without redesigning everything. Consistent templates make that easy."])]),
("when-should-you-redesign-your-website","When Should You Redesign Your Website?","Digital Trends","2026-09-04","Signs that a refresh is worth the effort, and signs it is not.",[
("Signs it is time",["The site looks dated next to competitors, is hard to use on phones, loads slowly or no longer matches what you offer."]),
("Signs a smaller fix will do",["If the structure and message are sound, updated content, new images and a speed pass may be enough."]),
("How to approach it",["Review what works, keep valuable page addresses, plan redirects and set a clear goal for the new site before design begins."])]),
("essential-features-of-a-business-website","Essential Features of a Business Website","Branding","2026-09-02","The practical features almost every business site should include.",[
("The basics",["A clear description of what you do, easy contact options, a mobile-friendly layout and readable text."]),
("Trust signals",["Real examples of your work, honest information about how you operate and consistent branding."]),
("Foundations behind the scenes",["Page titles and descriptions, image descriptions for accessibility, fast loading and a privacy policy that matches what the site actually does."])])]
